    "notes": "The sheltered portal retains the raised gable tips, diagonal reed courses under the soffit and carved passage. The two deep asymmetric clay recesses follow the entrance photo. A curved clay return joins the left jamb and leaves a route around its rounded end. The concrete apron connects the roadside arch to the portal and supports the iron leaves. The revised angle separates the roadside leaves from the shelter and matches the views from inside the approach. The two iron leaves show distinct photographed reliefs. The left leaf carries a scaled fish-tailed figure, seated drummer, hooded figure behind two bowls and a kneeling bearer under the round finial. The right leaf carries draped musicians, an oval mask and an incised vessel. The folded metal, scale rows, rolled bowl lips and rounded crowns read in the close views. The tall roadside arch and low wall have bowls and rounded lips cut into one clay surface. The sculpted cavities vary in depth, tilt and size. Fine marks and concealed construction remain estimated."
